            <h1 class="feature-video__title ">
                'I had to learn to walk again': Eliza's road back from spinal injury
            </h1>

                <p class="feature-video__summary ">Melbourne winger Eliza McNamara opens up about the serious spinal injury she suffered in 2022, and her journey back to the playing field</p>
        </div>
    </div>
    </div>
</div><h4>SATURDAY, SEPTEMBER 2</h4>
<p><strong>Carlton v Gold Coast at Ikon Park, 1.05pm AEST</strong> </p>
<p>Carlton is the first – and only – inaugural side the Suns have beaten. The win, which took place in round nine last season, was a turning of the tide in the matchup, after Gold Coast lost its first two outings against the Blues by 60 and 30 points respectively. Star midfielder Charlie Rowbottom gathered 26 disposals and five clearances for the Suns, while former Blue Lucy McEvoy had 24 disposals. </p><div class="articleWidget center">


        <section
            id="e2e539ef-1f36-4d24-bc77-63df9c046f8e"
            class="content-link embeddable-widget embeddable-widget--full-width-mobile "
        >
            <a class="content-link__link" href="/aflw/news/1020361/skipper-comes-through-blues-review-excited-for-the-future" target="_blank">
                <div class="content-link__category-wrapper">
	<svg class="icon " aria-hidden="true">
			<use xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink" xlink:href="/resources/v5.54.8/i/svg-output/icons.svg#icn-news"></use>
	</svg>
                    <div class="content-link__category">NEWS</div>
	<svg class="icon content-link__category-wrapper-edge" aria-hidden="true">
			<use xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink" xlink:href="/resources/v5.54.8/i/svg-output/icons.svg#icn-content-label-edge"></use>
	</svg>
                </div>
                <div class="content-link__title"><span class="content-link__title-text">Skipper comes through Blues review excited for the future</span>	<svg class="icon content-link__link-icon" aria-hidden="true">
			<use xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink" xlink:href="/resources/v5.54.8/i/svg-output/icons.svg#icn-arrow-right"></use>
	</svg>
</div>
            </a>
        </section>
</div><p>Gold Coast, which will unveil exciting midfielder Alana Gee on Saturday, is coming off its most successful season to date in which it won five games and finished ninth on the ladder. From here, it must show improvement again, maintaining that positive trajectory and against a Blues side that is playing its first game under a new coach and leaning heavily on the talent of its youth, it is the perfect opportunity to start the season with a win. </p>
<p><strong>Tip:</strong> Alana Gee will score a win on debut. Gold Coast by five points. </p><div class="articleWidget center">


    <figure id="47e45c60-de20-4577-9adb-bfd5669b2fc9" class="photo  embeddable-widget embeddable-widget--floating embeddable-widget--full-width-mobile " data-widget="lazy-load-images">
        <div class="photo__container">
            <div class="photo__wrapper placeholder placeholder--dark placeholder--medium">
    <div class="js-lazy-load lazy-image-wrapper  ">
                <!--         <picture class="photo__img object-fit-cover-picture ">
                    <source class="" srcset="https://resources.afl.com.au/photo-resources/2023/08/08/02ce4230-a96f-4c03-9576-0ca11e8f8bf9/xcjjh4MH.jpg?width=410&height=230, https://resources.afl.com.au/photo-resources/2023/08/08/02ce4230-a96f-4c03-9576-0ca11e8f8bf9/xcjjh4MH.jpg?width=820&height=460 2x, https://resources.afl.com.au/photo-resources/2023/08/08/02ce4230-a96f-4c03-9576-0ca11e8f8bf9/xcjjh4MH.jpg?width=1230&height=690 3x" media="(max-width: 425px)">
                    <source class="" srcset="https://resources.afl.com.au/photo-resources/2023/08/08/02ce4230-a96f-4c03-9576-0ca11e8f8bf9/xcjjh4MH.jpg?width=745&height=420, https://resources.afl.com.au/photo-resources/2023/08/08/02ce4230-a96f-4c03-9576-0ca11e8f8bf9/xcjjh4MH.jpg?width=1490&height=840 2x, https://resources.afl.com.au/photo-resources/2023/08/08/02ce4230-a96f-4c03-9576-0ca11e8f8bf9/xcjjh4MH.jpg?width=2235&height=1260 3x" media="(max-width: 768px)">
