            <p>CLASSY North Melbourne midfielder Jasmine Garner dictated play from the first few seconds of the match as the Kangaroos charged to a comfortable 40-point opening round win over St Kilda at Blundstone Arena on Sunday.</p>
<p>The Kangaroos scored the first 37 points of the game and kept the Saints scoreless in the first half on their way to recording the 8.8 (56) to 2.4 (16) victory.</p>
<p><strong>KANGAROOS v SAINTS <a href="https://www.afl.com.au/aflw/matches/5748" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Full match coverage and stats</a></strong></p>
<p>The Saints came out snarling after half-time, but inaccurate kicking meant they only outscored North by nine points to trail by 27 going into the final quarter.</p><div class="articleWidget center">

